exports[`Newy > /start 1`] = `
"## Hi, I'm Newy 😊

I'm here to help you keep up with the topics you care about. Use the Chat tab to talk with me directly — every other tab is one I push to and don't answer in, so what you're reading stays tidy.

What I do:

- **Chat** — chat with me about anything, ask for details, or follow up on an article 📰.
- I keep our conversation in one place so your context stays intact.

- **One tab per beat** — each subject you follow gets its own 📅, and its digests go there and nowhere else.

- **Translations** — where /translearn and /translate put an article once you've asked for it 📜.

Beats:

- 🧠 Computer Science
- 🎨 Design

A beat's tab appears the first time it has something to send you, so a brand new one is quiet until then. \`/pause\` closes a tab without deleting anything in it, and \`/resume\` opens it again.

Digests arrive at 10:00, 20:00 Europe/Paris. Each article is delivered as its own message so you can read or save what matters.

Commands:

**Reading**
- \`/start\` — this message.
- \`/summarize\` — a detailed summary of the article. In English by default — add a language to get it in that one: \`/summarize fr\`.
- \`/translearn\` — the article in your language, with the English behind every word worth learning.
- \`/translate\` — the article in your language, with only the key terms shown in English.

**Beats**
- \`/follow\` — follow a new subject. Say it in any language and I set the beat up and go looking for feeds. \`/follow formula 1\`.
- \`/beats\` — the beats I follow, with their feeds and what they did this week.
- \`/beat\` — one beat in full — its rubric, its feeds, its thresholds. \`/beat design\`.
- \`/pause\` — stop a beat without losing it — nothing is deleted. \`/pause design\`.
- \`/resume\` — start a paused beat again. \`/resume design\`.
- \`/addfeed\` — add an RSS feed to a beat. I check it before saving it. \`/addfeed design <url>\`.
- \`/removefeed\` — stop a beat pulling from a feed. Its old articles stay. \`/removefeed design <url>\`.
- \`/why\` — swipe an article and ask why it was sent — or why it was not.

The reading commands work on a swipe: reply to any article and send \`/summarize\`, \`/why\` or a translation on its own. The beat commands don't need one — they take a slug, and \`/beats\` lists them.

\`/why\` is the one worth knowing about: every beat scores every article it sees and writes down what it made of it, so you can swipe something and ask why it arrived — or swipe one I skipped and see what it scored.

\`/translearn\` and \`/translate\` answer in your own language, with the English kept in view, in the Translations tab — a long article arrives as several messages over a few minutes.

\`/summarize\` answers here in Chat, as one message: the article explained properly rather than compressed. It writes in English unless you name a language after it — \`/summarize fr\`, \`/summarize ru\`, or the language's own name.

**YouTube links need no command at all** 🎬 — paste one here and I'll read its transcript and explain what's actually in it, in your language. It works on a two-hour talk as well as a five-minute one; if a video has no captions there's nothing I can read, and I'll say so rather than guess.

If you want something specific, just ask — search the archive, show me a recent article, or tell me what interests you 😉."
`;

